DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The  uuaallaarrmm()  function causes the signal SSIIGGAALLRRMM to be sent to the in‐
       voking process after (not less than) _u_s_e_c_s microseconds.  The delay may
       be lengthened slightly by any system activity or by the time spent pro‐
       cessing the call or by the granularity of system timers.

       Unless caught  or  ignored,  the  SSIIGGAALLRRMM  signal  will  terminate  the
       process.

       If  the  _i_n_t_e_r_v_a_l  argument is nonzero, further SSIIGGAALLRRMM signals will be
       sent every _i_n_t_e_r_v_a_l microseconds after the first.

